#  DWD ICON global open data, AFTER gdt101_remap has put each record on a
#  regular latitude-longitude grid (the native product is GRIB2 grid
#  template 101, which this writer does not read).  Authored from the real
#  2026-10-11 12Z step-0 bytes through grib2_inventory (centre 78, local
#  table 1).  Use with --map-source dwd.
#  Soil temperature T_SO is published at TERRA's nodes, each the midpoint
#  of a layer, on type 106 with no second surface; GRIB2 carries the depth
#  in metres, the Level1 column carries it in cm rounded as this writer
#  rounds it (0.005 m -> 1), and Level2 is the missing second surface (0).
#  The SOILTnnn names are the init's TERRA layer names (nnn = layer
#  thickness in cm, 999 for 1458).
#  Soil water W_SO is a MASS per layer (kg m-2) on type 106 depth pairs.
#  SOILW is scratch (blank description); the blank-selector SOILM rows
#  declare the writer's SOILM = SOILW / (1000 x layer thickness) output.
#  Terrain is HSURF in metres directly; the land field is FR_LAND, a
#  fraction, which the dwd map-source row flags at 0.5.  2 m humidity is
#  dewpoint (scratch); the writer derives RH.  Pressure-level RELHUM is over
#  water, so the dwd row leaves the over-ice conversion off.
#  Geopotential FI becomes HGT through the GEOPT rule.
